  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The embolism: the prayer takes up the last petition just answered — líbera nos a malo — and expands it into all evils past, present and to come. Its conclusion is said over the breaking of the Host, which is why the rubrics fall where they do: the Host is broken in two at Per eúndem Dóminum nostrum Iesum Christum Fílium tuum, a particle is broken from the left half at Qui tecum vivit et regnat, and only Per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum is said aloud. PRÆTÉRITIS, PRÆSÉNTIBUS and FUTÚRIS (w008-w011) are tagged adjectives, not participles: both analyzers head prætéritus, præsens and futúrus as adjectives in their own right, the reverse of the case at ordinarium.qui-pridie w014. ADIÚTI at w044 is a participle of adiuvo, not an adjective; both analyzers head the form there. OPE at w041 is the ablative of ops, a noun with no nominative singular in use. GENETRÍCE at w020 is an adjudicated orthographic variant against witness handmissal-eo (see the apparatus).",
